    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "386f1853-7040-368e-a1a3-5afe5cc4b630",
                "word": "eftsoons",
                "pos": "adv",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4fc479fc-70af-3dc8-8eb6-fe3309ce835a",
                        "entry_id": "386f1853-7040-368e-a1a3-5afe5cc4b630",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Once again; another time."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "literary",
                            "not-comparable",
                            "obsolete",
                            "sometimes"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3aa7eae9-e1cf-4d54-9f3a-43358ad2acd7",
                                "sense_id": "4fc479fc-70af-3dc8-8eb6-fe3309ce835a",
                                "text": "And every day, when the convent of this abbey hath eaten, the almoner let bear the relief to the garden, and he smiteth on the garden gate with a clicket of silver that he holdeth in his hand; and anon all the beasts of the hill and of diverse places of the garden come out a 3000, or a 4000; and they come in guise of poor men, and men give them the relief in fair vessels of silver, clean over-gilt. And when they have eaten, the monk smiteth eftsoons on the garden gate with the clicket, and then anon all the beasts return again to their places that they come from.."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "60af7b2b-3178-3249-8e93-9ba7e07ff0c5",
                        "entry_id": "386f1853-7040-368e-a1a3-5afe5cc4b630",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Soon after, presently."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic",
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bd82048e-7395-4122-a63e-90d74db9efc1",
                                "sense_id": "60af7b2b-3178-3249-8e93-9ba7e07ff0c5",
                                "text": "But wil you giue me leaue now eftsones a while to play the Sophister his part with you?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "38002726-e641-40ac-b92a-acfc12e2621a",
                                "sense_id": "60af7b2b-3178-3249-8e93-9ba7e07ff0c5",
                                "text": "Now ſtands the Brere like a Lord alone, / Puffed up with pryde and vaine pleaſaunce: / But all this glee had no continuaunce. / For eftſoones Winter gan to approche, / The bluſtring Boreas did encroche, / And beate upon the ſolitarie Brere: / For nowe no ſuccour was ſeene him neere."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "82fc74a7-c406-4402-a9b8-bb9a55457bb4",
                                "sense_id": "60af7b2b-3178-3249-8e93-9ba7e07ff0c5",
                                "text": "He holds him with his skinny hand, / “There was a ship,” quoth he. / “Hold off! unhand me, grey-beard loon!” / Eftsoons his hand dropt he."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a2ab5f69-9d82-4d3e-a0d0-a69dcd70ad97",
                                "sense_id": "60af7b2b-3178-3249-8e93-9ba7e07ff0c5",
                                "text": "[…] but when the world is really wise—may that day come eftsoons!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3f5e34ff-9344-44c0-85da-72b94acb9ad1",
                                "sense_id": "60af7b2b-3178-3249-8e93-9ba7e07ff0c5",
                                "text": "Princess Scarlet fanned herself with the Chinese fan that Supply had provided and, turning to Achmed Ali, said in formal tones, \"Belike, sir, I've not seen thy match for overall all-in dancing eftsoons."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5c4ac069-6dd6-4d05-bead-7d5ea31ae03b",
                                "sense_id": "60af7b2b-3178-3249-8e93-9ba7e07ff0c5",
                                "text": "\"Eftsoons he will speak unto you,\" warned the mummy formally; […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
